      "id": "BLOCK_V11_EXACT_ADAPTER_MODULE_OBJECT_NOT_BOUND",
      "area": "typed_memory_adapter_import_identity_and_toctou",
      "detail": "The installer validates the path and SHA-256 of the file named by module.__file__ and only the current callable's __name__. It does not prove that the supplied/imported Python object is the canonical module executed from those bytes. A forged object naming the genuine file is accepted. V11 prepare_live_memory_integration also accepted the forged object after package/sys.modules substitution and returned installed=true, while real preserved-byte and V10-audit checks ran.",
      "why_blocking": "V11's central integration claim is exact installation into the sealed v8 adapter. The reproduced path can emit affirmative evidence while patching a different object, so exact object identity, TOCTOU closure, and evidence truth are not established.",
      "required_repair": "Use an append-only successor that establishes and retains the canonical adapter module object in a clean child before any substitutable import state, verifies module name/spec/origin/loader plus exact source bytes and the original callable identity, revalidates immediately at patch time, and rejects any pre-existing or replaced module object. Prefer an exact sealed successor adapter over runtime monkeypatching. Add the two reproduced probes and require another different fresh static audit."
    }
  ],
